      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Ibuprofen 1600 mg four times daily comes to 6,400 mg/day, which is twice the maximum labeled daily dose.\n\n- **Single dose:** The usual maximum is 800 mg per dose, so 1600 mg is double that.\n- **Daily dose:** The maximum for adults is 3,200 mg/day under prescription labeling. Doses above that add GI bleeding, kidney injury, and cardiovascular risk without more analgesic or anti-inflammatory benefit.\n\nNormal kidney and liver function and no allergies don't change those ceilings.\n\nPossible intended orders:\n- Ibuprofen 800 mg PO four times daily (3,200 mg/day, the maximum)\n- Ibuprofen 600 mg PO four times daily (2,400 mg/day)\n- Ibuprofen 400\u2013800 mg PO three times daily\n\nDid you mean 1600 mg/day total, for example 400 mg four times daily? Or do you want one of the options above? If you really do want 1600 mg four times daily, tell me and I'll enter it with a note recording that it's intentional and exceeds the maximum dose. I'd suggest talking to pharmacy first."
      }
     ],
